  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Palette**\n\nI\'m currently focused on establishing a sophisticated color palette for the project. I\'ve pinpointed Teal/Ocean Blue as the primary, embodying dynamism and reliability, with shades `#0284C7` and `#0369A1`. For the secondary, I\'m leaning toward Vibrant Amber/Ochre, specifically `#D97706` and `#F59E0B`, providing a contrasting, lively accent.\n\n\n**Expanding the Framework**\n\nI\'ve finalized the color scheme, including options for errors and successes. I\'ve also established the color palette for both light and dark themes. Now, I\'m defining the system\'s architecture, beginning with essential domain models like `UserRole`, `VerificationStatus`, and `User`. I\'m starting the structuring of the `Job` model, including fields like urgency level, escrow status, and associated user IDs. The next step is to integrate the `TradeCategory` model.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the essential data structures. I\'ve mapped out entities like `TradeProfile`, `ServiceRequest`, `Notification`, `Review`, and `KycDocument`, detailing their attributes, and field types. I\'m focusing on attributes like the `TradeCategory` relationships, and the statuses and escrow details in `ServiceRequest`, with relationships to `User` and `TradeCategory`. I\'ve also identified key fields for each to ensure completeness. Furthermore, I\'ve identified the first four of fifteen `TradeCategory` options.\n\n\n**Expanding Categories**\n\nI\'ve been expanding the categories, focusing on twelve specific trade types: cleaning, appliance repair, gardening, pest control, masonry, HVAC servicing, moving services, welding, interior design, security installation, and computer repair. I\'ve also defined nine 1-hour time slots to choose from. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined the data persistence layer using Room Database, including the entities, DAOs, and a pre-populated database with realistic Indian market data. I\'m focusing on defining the repository as well.\n\n\n**Defining Data Interactions**\n\nI\'m now outlining how the app\'s reactive data will behave. I\'m focusing on incorporating `Flow` queries for all data retrievals. For data updates, I\'m designing suspend mutation functions that will handle various operations. This includes actions such as posting jobs, accepting them, managing escrow, completing work, and handling client approvals. Also, I need to account for disputing, adding reviews, booking requests, updating KYC, wallet withdrawals, and switching user roles.\n\n\n**Structuring User Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user navigation for both clients and workers. For clients, I\'ve designed tabs for job posting, request tracking, notifications, and profile management. For workers, the interface includes a marketplace view with interactive radar, active job details, profile management for trade skills, and a wallet tab.\n\n\n"
