  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "# Updated Session Summary\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Build an Android app (\"Sahaya\"):** A two-sided trade services marketplace connecting clients with skilled workers.\n  - **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION.\n  - **Details:** The data layer and core UI components/screens are scaffolded. The next phase is to integrate the navigation logic in `MainActivity` and implement the remaining worker-specific screens and business logic flows.\n- **Navigation Implementation:** The user requires a functional navigation system that switches between screens based on the `SahayaViewModel` state.\n- **Worker-side Implementation:** While many screens are created, the worker-specific dashboard, active job management, and wallet features need further integration and refinement.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **App Concept:** \"Two-sided trade services marketplace connecting clients with skilled workers for home repairs, emergency services, and escrow bookings.\"\n- **App Name:** \"Sahaya\"\n- **Design Preferences:** Use of specific brand colors: Rich Ocean Blue (`SahayaPrimary`), Craftsman Gold (`SahayaAmber`), and Deep Verified Teal (`SahayaTeal`).\n- **Language Support:** The app must support a toggle between English and Hindi.\n- **Architecture:** The user prefers the MVVM pattern with Room for persistence and `StateFlow` for reactive UI updates.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Theme & Styling:** Updated `Color.kt` and `Theme.kt` with the custom Sahaya color palette.\n- **State Management:** Created `SahayaViewModel.kt` to act as the single source of truth for navigation, user session, and business logic.\n- **UI Components:** Created a suite of reusable components:\n  - `StatusBadge.kt` (Urgency, JobStatus, EscrowStatus, VerificationStatus)\n  - `EscrowStatusBar.kt` (Payment progress timeline)\n  - `StarRating.kt` (Display and Input)\n  - `TradeIcons.kt` (Category icon mapping)\n  - `JobCard.kt` & `WorkerCard.kt` (List items)\n  - `RazorpayPaymentDialog.kt` (Escrow payment simulation)\n  - `InteractiveJobMap.kt` (Canvas-based radar map for jobs)\n- **Screens:** Created the following screens:\n  - **Auth:** `LandingScreen`, `LoginScreen`, `RegisterScreen`\n  - **Client:** `ClientDashboardScreen`, `PostJobScreen`\n  - **Shared:** `KYCUploadScreen`, `VerificationPendingScreen`, `NotificationsScreen`, `ProfileScreen`\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:** The app uses MVVM. `SahayaViewModel` holds `StateFlow` objects for `currentScreen` and various data streams (jobs, profiles, notifications).\n- **Navigation:** Navigation is state-driven. The `MainActivity` should observe `SahayaViewModel.currentScreen` to determine which composable to display.\n- **Concurrency:** Repository methods are `suspend` functions; UI layer uses `viewModelScope` to launch coroutines.\n- **Data Flow:** The `SahayaRepository` exposes `Flow` streams from the Room database, which the ViewModel converts to `StateFlow` using `stateIn`.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n#### Edited Files\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/theme/Color.kt`: Defined brand-specific colors.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/theme/Theme.kt`: Applied new colors to `LightColorScheme` and `DarkColorScheme`.\n\n#### Created Files\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/viewmodel/SahayaViewModel.kt`: Central state and logic hub.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/`:\n  - `StatusBadge.kt`, `EscrowStatusBar.kt`, `StarRating.kt`, `TradeIcons.kt`, `JobCard.kt`, `WorkerCard.kt`, `RazorpayPaymentDialog.kt`, `InteractiveJobMap.kt`.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/auth/`:\n  - `LandingScreen.kt`, `LoginScreen.kt`, `RegisterScreen.kt`.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/client/`:\n  - `ClientDashboardScreen.kt`, `PostJobScreen.kt`.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/screens/shared/`:\n  - `KYCUploadScreen.kt`, `VerificationPendingScreen.kt`, `NotificationsScreen.kt`, `ProfileScreen.kt`.\n\n#### Viewed Files\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt`: The entry point that needs to be updated to host the navigation logic.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/repository/SahayaRepository.kt`: Referenced for ViewModel data access.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Work:** The UI screens and ViewModel are ready.\n- **Next Steps:**\n  1.  **Navigation Integration:** Update `MainActivity.kt` to implement a `NavHost` or a `when` block that switches screens based on `SahayaViewModel.currentScreen`.\n  2.  **Worker Screens:** Implement the remaining worker-specific screens (e.g., `WorkerMarketplaceScreen`, `ActiveJobScreen`, `WalletScreen`).\n  3.  **Integration:** Connect the `PostJobScreen` and `LoginScreen` to the `SahayaViewModel` methods to ensure data flows correctly to the database.\n- **Relevant Skills:**\n  - `/skills/system_skills/design_guidelines/SKILL.md`: Continue to follow M3 guidelines for all new UI components."
    included_step_index_start: 66
    included_step_index_end: 107
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/26437d04-f70c-4083-9dd2-27925dfa8548/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
  }
